  "description": "NIPLAA crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C6 H16 N1 1+,C123 H94 Cl1 N3 O28 Tm5 1-,2.5(C7 H8). From the CIF bond table, Tm1 (Tm) has 8 O neighbors; Tm2 (Tm) has 8 O neighbors; Tm3 (Tm) has 8 O neighbors; Tm4 (Tm) has 8 O neighbors; Tm5 (Tm) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.462-5.045 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.84-160.36°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula HNEt3[Tm5(μ3-OH)4(μ4-OH)(Ph2acac)7(o-O2NC6H4O)3Cl]·2.5C7H8. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
